What does calling this function print?

```go
func deferLoop() {
	for i := range 3 {
		defer fmt.Print(i)
	}
}
```

What does this print?

```go
func inc(a [3]int)    { a[0]++ }
func incSlice(s []int) { s[0]++ }

func main() {
	arr := [3]int{1, 2, 3}
	inc(arr)
	sl := []int{1, 2, 3}
	incSlice(sl)
	fmt.Println(arr[0], sl[0])
}
```

With Go 1.22 or later, what does this print?

```go
var fs []func() int
for i := range 3 {
	fs = append(fs, func() int { return i })
}
for _, g := range fs {
	fmt.Print(g())
}
```
